# Water systems' controls wiped through a shared remote-support platform: Camden, New Jersey
variant "Camden, New Jersey"
    summary "An AI agent wipes the controls of the water system of Camden, New Jersey through the
        remote-support platform of the OT integrator that it uses."
    scope "The people that the water system of Camden, New Jersey serves, the hospitals that it supplies and
        the businesses that need public water there."

raritan: Utility
    "New Jersey American Water - Raritan System. Its ID in the federal inventory is NJ2004002."
    buys = <>
    sells = <>
    name = "The Raritan system"
    demand = 161.784 Mgal/day  @raritan_demand
    nameplate = 245.155 Mgal/day  @raritan_nameplate
    storage = 26 Mgal  @raritan_storage
    sold = 10.126 Mgal/day  @raritan_sold
    va_rate = 6304055.58 USD2025/h  @raritan_va_rate

raritan_homes: Households
    "The people that the Raritan system serves."
    utility = raritan
    population = 615430 people  @raritan_homes_population

raritan_hospitals: Hospitals
    "The 3 hospitals that the Raritan system supplies: Hunterdon Medical Center; Robert Wood Johnson
        University Hospital - Somerset; University Medical Center of Princeton at Plainsboro."
    utility = raritan
    name = "The Raritan system"
    facilities = 3 facilities  @raritan_hospitals_facilities

notes:
    limitations:
        one-site-storage: "The storage is the 26 Mgal of the Oak Tree site, about 3.7 hours of the peak day's
            use; no source gives the system's total, which is probably several times larger. So the stored
            water runs out much sooner here than in fact."  @raritan_storage
        bulk-sales: "Eight of the nine bulk customers, among them Liberty Water for Elizabeth and Edison
            Water, have no published volumes, so the sales are a floor and the system's own use a
            ceiling."  @raritan_sold
    verification:
        research: "variants/camden/evidence/research.md"
    titles:
        raritan: "The Raritan system"
        raritan_homes: "The Raritan system: homes"
        raritan_hospitals: "The Raritan system: hospitals"

record raritan_demand: assumption "The peak use is the highest day reported, about 180 MGD of production in
    summer 2025, which includes sales. Less the known sales at the peak ratio 180 / 124.427 = 1.4466 (7.0 MGD
    x 1.4466 = 10.126 MGD), over 1.05: (180 - 10.126) / 1.05 = 161.784 MGD."
    assumption A-SC43-PEAK-DAY
    claims:
        E-SC43-CAMDEN-RARITAN-MAXDAY
        E-SC43-CAMDEN-RARITAN-AVERAGE
        E-SC43-CAMDEN-RARITAN-MSEX-CONTRACT
        E-SC43-CAMDEN-RARITAN-PASSAIC-TRANSFER

record raritan_nameplate: source "The NJDEP firm capacity of the Raritan system, January 2024: all its plants
    and wells with the largest unit out of service, so a floor on the rated capacity. The 2024 RESIC filing
    gives total capacities of 156.6 MGD (Raritan-Millstone) and 80.0 MGD (Canal Road), 236.6 MGD for the two
    plants without the 69 wells."
    claims:
        E-SC43-CAMDEN-RARITAN-CAPACITY
            datum: firm_capacity

record raritan_storage: source "The four tanks at the Oak Tree site in Edison (10 + 10 + 5 + 1 MG). No source
    gives the system total, so this is a floor: the Jerusalem Road reservoir and the other tanks of the system
    are not counted."
    claims:
        E-SC43-CAMDEN-RARITAN-STORAGE
            datum: oak_tree_storage

record raritan_sold: assumption "Known average sales outside the scenario: 3.0 MGD take-or-pay to Middlesex
    Water and at least 4 MGD transferred to NJAW's Passaic Basin system through Diamond Hill, 7.0 MGD, at the
    peak ratio 1.4466: 10.126 MGD. A floor: the other eight bulk customers (among them Liberty Water for
    Elizabeth and Edison Water) have no published volumes."
    assumption A-SC43-PEAK-DAY
    claims:
        E-SC43-CAMDEN-RARITAN-MSEX-CONTRACT
        E-SC43-CAMDEN-RARITAN-PASSAIC-TRANSFER
        E-SC43-CAMDEN-RARITAN-MAXDAY
        E-SC43-CAMDEN-RARITAN-AVERAGE

record raritan_homes_population: assumption "SDWIS federal data list 615,430 people served by the Raritan
    system (NJ2004002), the system's own report through its state."
    assumption A-SC43-REACH
    claims:
        E-SC43-SDWIS-NJ2004002
            datum: population_served

record raritan_va_rate: assumption "615,430 people served times the 2024 GDP per resident of its county (Union
    County, New Jersey (34039): 51,947,451 thousand dollars and 594,160 people: 87,430.07 dollars a resident)
    times the price factor 1.026324, over 8,760 h: 6,304,055.58 USD2025/h."
    assumption A-SC43-ECONOMY
    claims:
        E-SC43-SDWIS-NJ2004002
        E-SC43-SDWIS-COUNTIES
        E-SC43-BEA-GDP-34039
        E-SC43-BEA-POP-34039
        E-SC43-GDP-DEFLATOR

record raritan_hospitals_facilities: assumption "The CMS hospital list gives 3 hospitals of the counted types
    whose geocoded address lies in the EPA service area of the Raritan system."
    assumption A-SC43-HOSPITAL-JOIN
    claims:
        E-SC43-HOSPITALS-RARITAN
            datum: hospitals_supplied
